# Copy to mobile/.env and fill in. Everything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the JS
# bundle, so it is visible to anyone with the app: never put a secret here.
#
# Where the Simple PM server is. Use your laptop's LAN IP, NOT localhost: on the phone
# "localhost" is the phone itself, so the request never leaves the device. Find yours with
# `ipconfig getifaddr en0` (macOS) or `hostname -I` (Linux), and use the same port your
# backend runs on (PORT in the repo-root .env, 3000 by default).
#
# The phone and the laptop must be on the same Wi-Fi, and the server must also trust this
# origin: add it to MOBILE_TRUSTED_ORIGINS in the repo-root .env.
#
# Restart Expo after changing this (`bun start --clear`); the value is baked in at bundle time.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3000
